{# THE AREA SETTINGS SECTION — what this area is, and what an installation may
   change about it.

   A SECTION, NOT A SCREEN. It carries no page frame, no head, no strip and no
   way back: the shell's configure page draws all four, and the area's Configure
   action is both the way in and the way out. Before the frame this was a screen
   of its own with a tab in the area's strip, which put "what this area is" beside
   "what is happening in it" as though the two were the same kind of place.

   GATED ON `areas.configure`, ASKED OF THE AREA by the declaration that lists
   this section, so reaching the section at all is the permission. The page states what is editable and what is not rather than
   offering fields that do nothing: the boundary is not re-drawn here, because
   importing one is a surface this bundle does not ship yet and pretending
   otherwise would be a form that fails on submit.

   THE SHEET IS LINKED HERE, IN THE BODY, and that is deliberate rather than
   sloppy: a section is included into a page the shell owns, and the shell's head
   cannot know which bundle's vocabulary the section is written in. A stylesheet
   link in the body is applied exactly as one in the head is; what it costs is
   that this section's own rules land a beat after the frame's. #}
{{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
<div class="grid">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">The record<span class="src">&middot; area_of_interest</span></span>

            {# READ-ONLY HERE, EDITED ON ITS OWN SCREEN. The record below is the
               lead; the one action is the door to the edit screen — including the
               boundary, which is never re-drawn on this page. #}
            <div class="id-head">
                <span class="id-lead">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
                    <span><b>Read-only here.</b> These facts are edited on their own screen &mdash; including the boundary.</span>
                </span>
                <a class="cta id-edit" href="{{ path('area_edit', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.12 2.12 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"/></svg> Edit area
                </a>
            </div>

            <table class="tbl">
                <tr><th>Name</th><td>{{ area.name }}</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Boundary source</th><td>{% if area.hasBoundary %}{{ area.source }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Size</th><td class="num">{{ areaKm2|number_format }} km&sup2;</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Zones</th><td class="num">{{ zoneCount > 0 ? zoneCount : '—' }}</td></tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>IUCN category</th>
                    <td>{% if area.iucnCategory %}{{ area.iucnCategory }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Established</th>
                    <td>{% if area.establishedYear %}{{ area.establishedYear }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Zone overlap tolerance</th>
                    <td class="num">{{ area.zoneOverlapTolerancePct ?? defaultZoneOverlapTolerance }} %{% if area.zoneOverlapTolerancePct is null %} <span class="chip">default</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                {# HOW OFTEN THIS AREA'S HANDSETS REPORT — the area's fact, the
                   one number the handset, the live reading and the roster's
                   thresholds all count from. Edited on the edit screen with
                   the rest of this record. #}
                <tr>
                    <th>Ping every</th>
                    <td class="num">{{ pingEvery }}{% if area.pingIntervalMinutes is null %} <span class="chip">default</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr><th>Identifier</th><td class="mono">{{ area.uuidString }}</td></tr>
            </table>
            <div class="use">The registry fields are optional and a dash means UNRECORDED, not zero:
                an installation that drew its own boundary has no IUCN category and no gazettement
                year, and must not be made to invent them to save a record.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
